    description: "WI-gohok's SOURCE HALF, filed 2026-09-07 on the owner's directive to integrate\nthe open owner-facing questions into the arc. Sits at the arc tail (T8), after\nT2 (WI-dozul) because WI-dozul enlarges the population this property describes.\n\nTHE PARENT DECISION, already ruled and not reopened here. WI-gohok, owner\nruling 2026-08-27, option B: a config-driven flow REMAINS a true positive on\nthe correctness axis (measurement 0001's rubric is not relitigated and\ncomparability with 0001/0004/0005/0006 is preserved by construction), and a\nSECOND figure -- \"useful precision\" -- publishes alongside it, excluding\nconfigured-action flows. The amendment the owner accepted with it is the\nbinding constraint on this item: the exclusion is defined STRUCTURALLY, by the\nSHAPE of the path, never by a per-case severity or actionability judgement.\nAn \"is this interesting?\" test would surrender the objectivity the 0001 rubric\nexists for. WI-gohok's 2026-08-26 direction names the distinction: a value\nCOMPUTED INTO the sink's payload versus one that SELECTS the resource the sink\nacts on. That matches the standing ruling already in force (\"taint flows via\nIN-PROGRAM COMPUTATION, not a resource selected by it\").\n\nTHE GAP THIS ITEM CLOSES. The distinction has no home in the data. The\n2026-09-06 taint-label concept audit (Pair 1,\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-taint-label_09062026.md) found the same\nproperty at the SOURCE, where it is decidable per ROW with no path analysis at\nall: of the 324 catalogue names that mint untrusted_input (net_recv 89,\nipc_recv 148, db_read 87), 24 return a value the far side CHOSE FROM A\nCONSTRAINED SET rather than authored -- accept x10 (a peer address; c, erlang\ngen_tcp + ssl transport_accept, go x3, java, python x2, rust), erlang inet DNS\nx7, process exit status x7 (python os.wait* x5, rust Child.wait/try_wait).\nA choice-shaped source can only ever produce a SELECTS finding: an address, a\nname from a fixed table, or eight status bits cannot be \"computed into\" a shell\ncommand in the injection sense.\n\nNOT DERIVABLE FROM ANY EXISTING FIELD, which is why it must be its own\nproperty: net_recv holds BOTH recv (content) and accept (choice); ipc_recv\nholds BOTH check_output (content) and os.wait (choice). Boundary, kind and\nsource_boundary all cut across it.\n\nSTEP 1, AND IT GATES THE REST: SIZE IT FINDING-WEIGHTED. 24 of 324 is 7.4% of\ncatalogue NAMES. The share of FINDINGS that root in a choice-shaped source is\nNOT MEASURED and is the number that says whether this property is worth a\nfield. Measure it before building: count situations whose source primitive is\none of the 24 on the standing measurement cohort. A per-name share is not a\nper-finding share (LIVE rule 13 in its general form: the denominator is the\nclaim). If the finding-weighted share is negligible the honest outcome is a\ndated declared finding, not a field.\n\nFIX SHAPE, not designed here. A per-row `value_shape: content | choice` on\ncatalogue source rows, defaulting to content, with the 24 rows above stamped\nchoice. Under the field-axis rules this is a new axis declaration and must be\ndeclared BEFORE the field is added -- bounded-enum documented on the dataclass,\nor the lightweight catalog-derived route per ADR-0024 section 4; the\nmulti-value-field-axis playbook governs which. Every finding from a stamped row\ncarries SELECTS with zero sink-side analysis; the composition the audit\nproposes is finding_shape = choice-source OR selects-role, and the second\ndisjunct is the sibling item (the sink half).\n\nWHAT IT MUST NOT BE, both already refused on their own threads: NOT a label\nsplit (WI-vazal -- a label split silently flipped 3 of 16 verdicts and was\nrefused in favour of carrying origin) and NOT a boundary split (WI-dozul's\n2026-09-06 ruling). And it must NOT absorb vacuity that is a BUG rather than a\nrubric limit: all five shellcheck true positives are Haskell in-process\nIORef/STRef writes filed under untrusted-input-no-database, which is INV-nular\n(primitive kind asserted by name, never checked) and gets FIXED, not excluded.\nBoth classes produce \"true and vacuous\" findings and only one is a defect;\nconflating them would launder a bug through a rubric change. That exclusion is\nthe owner's, recorded verbatim on WI-gohok.\n\nMEASUREMENT HOOK, pre-registered by the audit: T2's (WI-dozul) 0003 delta is\nthe first number this property is judged on -- WI-dozul adds DNS rows in five\nmore languages and every one of them is choice-shaped, so it both enlarges the\npopulation and supplies the arm. Ship with the 0003 delta and\nawaits_bakeoff_validation like every other recall-adjacent PR.\n\nSEQUENCING CONSTRAINT INHERITED FROM THE PARENT: the owner ruled fix-then-\nbaseline with WI-gohok gating the series (WI-gohok -> INV-kakad + INV-sukoh\n-> INV-nular / INV-fumod remainders -> INV-duvup's pre-registered baseline).\nINV-duvup's statement requires the rubric FIXED IN ADVANCE of the first datum,\nso this must land before that baseline is taken or the series restarts."  # 284c
