  clock: 3  # 4997
  nonce: '4997'  # 4997
  message: "THE FINDING-WEIGHTED NUMBER THIS ITEM ASKED FOR, FIRST DATA POINT (arc T8).\nRecord: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jivih_t8_09112026/ (`size_findings.py`,\n`RESULT.md`). Computed from artifacts produced for T0c and T7; no new analysis\nrun was needed.\n\nThe item says: \"SIZED FINDING-WEIGHTED FIRST: 24 of 324 is a share of NAMES;\nthe share of FINDINGS is unmeasured and decides whether this earns a field or a\ndated declared blindness.\" The 2026-09-06 concept audit had already recorded\n\"Harm, honestly. Unmeasured.\"\n\n    repo                        findings  choice-shaped    share\n    pretix (python)                  125              0     0.0%\n    workadventure (ts/js)             18              0     0.0%\n    modsecurity (cpp/c)                0              0      n/a\n    apollo-server (ts)                 2              0     0.0%\n    TOTAL                            145              0     0.0%\n\n**0 of 145 findings carry a choice-shaped source.**\n\nAND THE ZERO IS CHECKED AGAINST A MISSING POPULATION, which is the whole risk\nhere. A zero has two causes licensing opposite conclusions: the rows exist and\nnever produce findings (the property is harmless), or the rows are never called\nin this corpus (the corpus cannot see the question). So io-boundary CHAINS were\ncounted too, independently of findings: workadventure 1585 chains / 0\nchoice-shaped, modsecurity 61 / 1, apollo-server 61 / 0. The single hit is\n`sys/wait.wait` on modsecurity, and it sits on the **`subprocess`** boundary --\na SINK -- not on one of the three source boundaries that mint\n`untrusted_input`, so it is not even an instance of the property.\n\n**THIS CORPUS CANNOT ANSWER THE QUESTION AND THE 0.0% MUST NOT BE READ AS \"THE\nPROPERTY IS HARMLESS\".** 17 of the 24 choice-shaped names live in go, java,\nerlang and rust -- `accept` in three of them, the whole erlang `inet` DNS\nfamily in the fourth -- and this corpus contains no repository in any of those\nlanguages. It was selected for a different measurement.\n\nWHAT A REAL SIZING NEEDS: a cohort with at least one SERVER in go, java, erlang\nand rust, run through `verify-claims` with the generic claims, counting findings\nwhose `source_primitives` last segment is in the choice set. The instrument is\nwritten, takes any set of `vc.json` artifacts, and runs in under a second; only\nthe cohort is missing.\n\nPREDICTION RECORDED BEFORE THAT COHORT RUNS, so it cannot be adjusted\nafterwards: if a corpus that CAN see the population also returns ~0 findings,\nthen a schema field on 324 catalogue rows is paid for by nothing and the dated\ndeclared blindness is the honest answer. This data point narrows the decision;\nit does not make it."  # 4997
